25:["$","h2","h2-3",{"className":"font-cyber text-lg text-cyber-blue mb-3 mt-5 border-b border-cyan-900/20 pb-2","children":"Orchestrating with n8n"}]
26:["$","p","p-6",{"className":"font-code text-sm text-cyber-blue-dim leading-relaxed mb-4","children":"For workflows that mix AI steps with external services (APIs, databases, webhooks), n8n is excellent. It provides visual workflow orchestration and handles:"}]
27:["$","ul","ul-0",{"className":"space-y-1 mb-4 ml-4","children":["\n",["$","li","li-0",{"className":"font-code text-sm text-cyber-blue-dim flex items-start gap-2","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"text-neon-pink mt-0.5","children":"▸"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"Retry logic and error routing"}]]}],"\n",["$","li","li-1",{"className":"font-code text-sm text-cyber-blue-dim flex items-start gap-2","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"text-neon-pink mt-0.5","children":"▸"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"Webhook triggers and scheduled runs"}]]}],"\n",["$","li","li-2",{"className":"font-code text-sm text-cyber-blue-dim flex items-start gap-2","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"text-neon-pink mt-0.5","children":"▸"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"HTTP requests to external APIs"}]]}],"\n",["$","li","li-3",{"className":"font-code text-sm text-cyber-blue-dim flex items-start gap-2","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"text-neon-pink mt-0.5","children":"▸"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"Database read/write nodes"}]]}],"\n"]}]
28:["$","p","p-7",{"className":"font-code text-sm text-cyber-blue-dim leading-relaxed mb-4","children":"I use a pattern where LangGraph handles the AI reasoning loop and n8n handles the surrounding orchestration — triggering the agent, routing its output to the right destination, and sending notifications."}]
29:["$","h2","h2-4",{"className":"font-cyber text-lg text-cyber-blue mb-3 mt-5 border-b border-cyan-900/20 pb-2","children":"The Planning Problem"}]
2a:["$","p","p-8",{"className":"font-code text-sm text-cyber-blue-dim leading-relaxed mb-4","children":"Simple agents work on single-step tasks. Real tasks require multi-step planning:"}]
2b:["$","ul","ul-1",{"className":"space-y-1 mb-4 ml-4","children":["\n",["$","li","li-0",{"className":"font-code text-sm text-cyber-blue-dim flex items-start gap-2","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"text-neon-pink mt-0.5","children":"▸"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"\"Research competitor pricing\" requires: identify competitors → scrape pricing pages → extract data → compare → summarize"}]]}],"\n",["$","li","li-1",{"className":"font-code text-sm text-cyber-blue-dim flex items-start gap-2","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"text-neon-pink mt-0.5","children":"▸"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"\"Schedule a meeting\" requires: check availability → find slot → send invites → add to calendar"}]]}],"\n"]}]
2c:["$","p","p-9",{"className":"font-code text-sm text-cyber-blue-dim leading-relaxed mb-4","children":"For complex plans, I use a two-level architecture:"}]
2d:["$","ol","ol-1",{"className":"space-y-1 mb-4 ml-4 list-decimal","children":["\n",["$","li","li-0",{"className":"font-code text-sm text-cyber-blue-dim flex items-start gap-2","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"text-neon-pink mt-0.5","children":"▸"}],["$","span",null,{"children":[["$","strong","strong-0",{"className":"text-cyber-blue font-bold","children":"Planner agent"}],": breaks the goal into subtasks"]}]]}],"\n",["$","li","li-1",{"className":"font-code text-sm text-cyber-blue-dim flex items-start gap-2","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"text-neon-pink mt-0.5","children":"▸"}],["$","span",null,{"children":[["$","strong","strong-0",{"className":"text-cyber-blue font-bold","children":"Executor agent"}],": executes each subtask, reporting results back to the planner"]}]]}],"\n"]}]
2e:["$","p","p-10",{"className":"font-code text-sm text-cyber-blue-dim leading-relaxed mb-4","children":"This is more expensive but significantly more reliable than a single agent trying to do everything."}]
2f:["$","h2","h2-5",{"className":"font-cyber text-lg text-cyber-blue mb-3 mt-5 border-b border-cyan-900/20 pb-2","children":"What Breaks in Production"}]
30:["$","p","p-11",{"className":"font-code text-sm text-cyber-blue-dim leading-relaxed mb-4","children":[["$","strong","strong-0",{"className":"text-cyber-blue font-bold","children":"1. Context window overflow"}],": agents accumulate tool results and the context grows until it hits the limit. Solution: summarize older results instead of retaining raw output."]}]
31:["$","p","p-12",{"className":"font-code text-sm text-cyber-blue-dim leading-relaxed mb-4","children":[["$","strong","strong-0",{"className":"text-cyber-blue font-bold","children":"2. Tool selection errors"}],": the agent calls the wrong tool or with wrong parameters. Solution: add a validation step before execution, and use structured output forcing for tool calls."]}]
32:["$","p","p-13",{"className":"font-code text-sm text-cyber-blue-dim leading-relaxed mb-4","children":[["$","strong","strong-0",{"className":"text-cyber-blue font-bold","children":"3. Infinite loops"}],": the agent keeps trying failed approaches. Solution: add a step counter and a \"reflect on failure\" node that forces a different strategy after N failed attempts."]}]
33:["$","p","p-14",{"className":"font-code text-sm text-cyber-blue-dim leading-relaxed mb-4","children":[["$","strong","strong-0",{"className":"text-cyber-blue font-bold","children":"4. Hallucinated tool outputs"}],": the model sometimes generates what it \"thinks\" a tool would return instead of actually calling it. Solution: enforce tool calling via the model's function-calling API, never via free-text generation."]}]
34:["$","h2","h2-6",{"className":"font-cyber text-lg text-cyber-blue mb-3 mt-5 border-b border-cyan-900/20 pb-2","children":"The Future of Agentic AI"}]
35:["$","p","p-15",{"className":"font-code text-sm text-cyber-blue-dim leading-relaxed mb-4","children":"The shift from single-call AI to multi-step agents is the biggest change in practical AI engineering right now. The tooling is maturing fast — LangGraph's persistence layer, n8n's growing integration library, and better LLM function-calling support make production agents increasingly viable. The hard problems are no longer AI problems — they're software engineering problems."}]
36:["$","span",null,{"className":"text-cyber-blue-dim mr-1","children":">"}]
